fc8a0ac3 lu-hybSPvkRi5N0YAKMbRAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA 98:82a7616e63686f727391da00452f55736572732f776f726b73706163652f576f726b73706163652f636170746e2f74657374732f636f675f6c6f61645f66696c655f746573742e676f3a313a312d38353a31ac616e737765724c656e677468d10593 Go test file (package tests_test) exercising the cog workspace API with four tests. TestCOGLoadFilesDeduplicatesConcurrentLoads builds a slice of 32 identical relative paths to fixtures/golang/baseproj/simple.go, calls c.LoadFiles once, asserts no error and that 32 results are returned, then asserts every returned pointer is the Same (pointer-identical) as the first — proving concurrent/duplicate loads of one path are deduplicated into a single shared file object. TestCOGLoadFileClearsInflightAfterError first calls LoadFile on a missing main.go in a temp workspace and expects an error, then writes the file and calls LoadFile again expecting success — verifying a failed load does not leave a stale inflight/cached error entry that would poison retries. TestCOGPersistReturns runs c.Persist() in a goroutine sending its error to a buffered channel and uses select with a 1-second time.After timeout to assert Persist returns promptly without error (guards against deadlock/hang). TestOpenCOGLoadsPersistedCache creates an observation (common.PrimaryHash key, NewObservationSchema, wrapped via cog.NewCOGObservation with empty FileRange slice), inserts it into c.ObservationCache, persists, then reopens the workspace with cog.OpenWorkspace and asserts the reloaded ObservationCache entry equals the original — verifying persistence round-trips the observation cache. All assertions use testify assert (no require).
fc8a0ac3 mALymw9IPD9i5N0YAKMbRAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA 99:82a7616e63686f727391da00462f55736572732f776f726b73706163652f576f726b73706163652f636170746e2f74657374732f636f675f6c6f61645f66696c655f746573742e676f3a37313a312d38343a32ac616e737765724c656e677468d10315 Test verifying the observation-cache persistence round-trip in the cog package. It creates a temp workspace, computes h := common.PrimaryHash("persisted-observation"), builds an ObservationSchema whose ID is h.String() with answer "persisted answer", and wraps it in a COGObservation via cog.NewCOGObservation with an empty []*common.FileRange. It then constructs a workspace with cog.NewWorkspace, directly inserts the observation into the exported ObservationCache map keyed by h, and asserts c.Persist() succeeds (writing cache state to disk). Finally it calls cog.OpenWorkspace on the same directory and asserts the freshly loaded workspace's ObservationCache[h] deep-equals the original COGObservation, proving OpenWorkspace deserializes previously persisted cache entries faithfully.
