fc8a0ac3 IUYn0Fm-prdi5N0YAKMbRAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA 89:82a7616e63686f727391da003c2f55736572732f776f726b73706163652f576f726b73706163652f636170746e2f706b672f7475692f7374617475732e676f3a33383a312d34363a32ac616e737765724c656e677468d1020a ReportStatus is a convenience helper that reports a status message through a context-scoped provider. It calls GetStatusProvider(ctx) to retrieve a status provider stored in the context; if none is present (ok is false) it silently no-ops and returns, otherwise it delegates to provider.ReportStatus(t, status) with the given StatusType and status string. This makes status reporting optional and decoupled: callers can invoke ReportStatus unconditionally without checking whether a provider was injected into the context.
